# Eyebrow → Heading spacing rule

The gap between an eyebrow label and the heading directly below it is **always 4px (`gap-1`)**.
This is a global, non-negotiable design token — do not override it per section.

---

## The one correct pattern

The eyebrow rule is a **24 × 2px horizontal gradient bar** (brand gradient, Blue → Navy).
Use the `eyebrow-rule` utility class — NOT a rounded pill or a dot.

```astro
{/* ✅ Eyebrow + heading only */}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
  <p class="flex items-center gap-2 font-body text-[11px] font-bold leading-4 tracking-[1.54px] text-accent uppercase">
    <span class="eyebrow-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Eyebrow label
  </p>
  <h2 class="font-display … text-heading uppercase">Section heading</h2>
</div>

{/* ✅ Eyebrow + heading + body paragraph */}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
  <p class="flex items-center gap-2 font-body text-[11px] font-bold leading-4 tracking-[1.54px] text-accent uppercase">
    <span class="eyebrow-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    Eyebrow label
  </p>
  <h2 class="font-display … text-heading uppercase">Section heading</h2>
  {/* Body text needs its own top margin — do NOT increase the container gap */}
  <p class="mt-3 font-body … text-banner-note md:mt-4">Body paragraph…</p>
</div>
```

### `eyebrow-rule` utility (defined in `tailwind.css`)
- `display: block` · `width: 24px` · `height: 2px` · `background: var(--gradient-brand)` · `border-radius: 1px`
- Figma node 152:637 — horizontal gradient rectangle, NOT a vertical dot or pill

---

## What NOT to do

```astro
{/* ❌ gap-4 makes eyebrow → heading 16px, not 4px */}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
  <p class="eyebrow">…</p>
  <h2>…</h2>
</div>

{/* ❌ gap-2 is still too much (8px) */}
<div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
  <p class="eyebrow">…</p>
  <h2>…</h2>
</div>

{/* ❌ mb-1 on the eyebrow itself — use gap-1 on the container instead */}
<p class="mb-1 eyebrow">…</p>
<h2>…</h2>

{/* ❌ pt-1 on the heading — use gap-1 on the container */}
<p class="eyebrow">…</p>
<h2 class="pt-1">…</h2>
```

---

## Spacing after the heading

| Sibling after heading | Class to use |
|---|---|
| Body / lead paragraph | `mt-3` (mobile) + `md:mt-4` |
| Subtitle / supporting text | `mt-2` |
| CTA button / link | `mt-4` or `mt-6` |
| Bordered divider only (no body) | use `border-b` + `pb-6` on the container — no extra `mt` needed |

---

## Where this rule already applies

| File | Section |
|---|---|
| `FAQs.astro` | Light-mode heading block |
| `CTABanner.astro` | Eyebrow + H2 + note |
| `PageHero.astro`, `FeatureColumns.astro`, `TagGrid.astro` | Eyebrow + heading blocks |
| All `src/pages/` using inline eyebrow patterns | same rule |

## TL;DR

- Container holding eyebrow + heading: **`gap-1`** — always.
- Body text that follows: **`mt-3`** (mobile), **`md:mt-4`** (desktop).
- Never raise `gap-*` on the container to make room for body text.
